  "source_files": {
   "CRD3MFA1": "xdos/caesar_cbf/Xentry/MB_PKW/Caesar/cbf/CRD3MFA1.cbf -> mined/CRD3MFA1.json"
  },
  "cross_reference": "CBF connection block: HSCAN (UDS, 500 kbit) 0x7E0/0x7E8, global id 0x441; diag variant Diag_3300h (1,041 DTCs, 1,648 data reads). The longitudinal CRD3.json (19 variants) is also mined for cross-reference."
 },
 "notes": [
  "Grading: every entry is 'candidate'. Nothing here has answered on a car yet; running the cla-w117.md steps promotes entries by adding a live_<vin> key exactly like backend/profiles/jlr/data/sdd_dids.json.",
  "Byte/bit offsets are relative to the positive-response payload AFTER the 62 <DID> header bytes.",
  "The cylinder_pressure family is the EU6 closed-loop-combustion glow-plug pressure sensing (6719..671C asynch volts, 6714 TDC correction). If those answer, per-cylinder compression during cranking is directly comparable; if they NRC-refuse, the car's build does not carry the sensors and the family is dropped without affecting the rest.",
  "6702 battery-voltage-at-start + 61D5 starter-relay + 61C8 start-active timestamp the crank phase of the cold-start capture (chatter job).",
  "The GMF2 guided-diagnosis trees are encrypted and NOT mined; everything here comes from the Caesar layer.",
  "Raw-corpora locations and the not-mined list live in docs/dataset-registry.md."
 ],
